The database is restricted to the backend network without a published host port.

## Docker Compose Configuration

```yaml
services:
  assetportal:
    image: httpd:2.4
    container_name: assets-web
    ports:
      - "8160:80"
    cpus: 0.7
    mem_limit: 384m
    restart: unless-stopped
    networks:
      - assets-front
      - assets-back
    privileged: false
    cap_drop:
      - ALL
    security_opt:
      - no-new-privileges:true
    depends_on:
      database:
        condition: service_healthy

  database:
    image: postgres:16
    container_name: assets-db
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: assetsdb
      POSTGRES_USER: assetuser
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD:?Set password}
    cpus: 0.6
    mem_limit: 640m
    restart: always
    networks:
      - assets-back
    volumes:
      - assets-data:/var/lib/postgresql/data
    healthcheck:
      test:
        - CMD
        - pg_isready
        - -U
        - assetuser
        - -d
        - assetsdb
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 5
      start_period: 20s

networks:
  assets-front:
    name: assets-front
    driver: bridge

  assets-back:
    name: assets-back
    driver: bridge

volumes:
  assets-data:
    name: assets-data
```

## Health Check Configuration

| Parameter | Configuration |
|---|---|
| Health Check Utility | pg_isready |
| Interval | 10 seconds |
| Timeout | 5 seconds |
| Retries | 5 |
| Start Period | 20 seconds |
| Startup Dependency | service_healthy |

The web service waits for PostgreSQL to report a healthy status during initial Compose startup.

Health checks provide additional visibility into database readiness and operational availability.

## Security Controls

| Control | Purpose |
|---|---|
| privileged: false | Avoid privileged execution |
| cap_drop: ALL | Remove Linux capabilities |
| no-new-privileges | Prevent privilege acquisition |
| Network segmentation | Restrict unnecessary communication |
| Resource limits | Control resource consumption |
| Database port isolation | Reduce direct database exposure |
| Health checks | Monitor database readiness |
| Named volumes | Maintain persistent storage |

## Deployment and Verification

```powershell
docker compose config --quiet
docker compose up -d
docker compose ps
docker stats --no-stream
docker network inspect assets-front
docker network inspect assets-back
docker logs assets-web
docker exec assets-db pg_isready -U assetuser -d assetsdb
```

Web service testing is performed using localhost on port 8160.

## Health Monitoring Verification

```powershell
docker inspect --format "{{.State.Health.Status}}" assets-db
docker inspect --format "{{json .State.Health}}" assets-db
docker compose stop database
docker compose ps -a
docker compose start database
docker compose ps
```

Monitor the database health status until PostgreSQL becomes healthy again.

Health-based startup dependencies do not automatically restart dependent services when the database becomes unhealthy.

## Persistent Storage and Recovery

| Parameter | Configuration |
|---|---|
| Database | assetsdb |
| Test Table | inventory |
| Original Volume | assets-data |
| Backup Directory | C:\AssetsBackup |
| Backup Archive | assets-data.tar.gz |
| Restored Volume | assets-restored |

The recovery procedure involves stopping PostgreSQL, creating a physical volume backup, restoring the archive into a separate volume and verifying the original database records.

The final Compose configuration uses assets-restored as an external volume after restoration.

